    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "title: PlatformerGames\n\nPlatformer games are a genre of video games
    where the core gameplay focuses on moving a character through environments by
    running, jumping, falling, and climbing between platforms. The main challenge
    usually comes from precise movement, timing, and avoiding obstacles or enemies.\r\n\r\nIn
    platformers, levels are often designed vertically or horizontally, requiring
    players to react quickly and master the game\u2019s physics, such as jump height,
    gravity, and movement speed. Hazards like gaps, spikes, moving platforms, and
    enemies are commonly used to increase difficulty.\r\n\r\nThis genre can be either
    2D or 3D. In 2D platformers, movement is typically limited to left, right, up,
    and down, while 3D platformers allow freer movement in a three-dimensional space,
    adding camera control and depth-based challenges.\r"
